{
  "summary": "Escapes backslashes in addition to quotes when formatting the Tor control `AUTHENTICATE` command string. Also adds a functional test case verifying password escaping against the mock Tor control server.",
  "problem": "When connecting to the Tor control port using `HASHEDPASSWORD` authentication, `bitcoind` formats the password as a quoted string and only escapes quotation marks. Any backslash in `-torpassword` is treated by Tor as an escape character, resulting in authentication failures or malformed commands when backslashes are present.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"Tested against Tor 0.4.9.12 with HashedControlPassword set for pa\\ss\"word\\: on master bitcoind logs 'tor: Authentication failed', with this change authentication succeeds and ADD_ONION creates the onion service.\""
  ],
